title><![CDATA[The Fruit Fly Of Babylon]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p>So, I was so downcast from the remigration thing (see below the paywall) that I had to go visit the Brueghels in the Kunsthistorisches Museum the next morning, before taking the train back to Budapest. That great Vienna temple of art has the world’s largest collection of works by Pieter Brueghel the Elder. I wrote something about that visit for…</p><p>URL: <a href="https://roddreher.substack.com/p/the-fruit-fly-of-babylon?utm_source=substack&utm_campaign=post_embed&utm_medium=web">https://roddreher.substack.com/p/the-fruit-fly-of-babylon?utm_source=substack&utm_campaign=post_embed&utm_medium=web</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://arnoldkling.substack.com/p/ai-links-3142026">AI Links, 3/14/2026</a></p>]]></description><link>https://roddreher.substack.com/p/the-fruit-fly-of-babylon?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_campaign=post_embed&amp;utm_medium=web</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://roddreher.substack.com/p/the-fruit-fly-of-babylon?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_campaign=post_embed&amp;utm_medium=web</guid><pubDate>Wed, 11 Mar 2026 15:08:40 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[If AI is a weapon, why don't we regulate it like one?]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p>If you haven’t heard about the fight between the AI company Anthropic and the U.S. Department of War, you should read about it, because it could be critical for our future — as a nation, but also as a species…</p><p>URL: <a href="https://www.noahpinion.blog/p/if-ai-is-a-weapon-why-dont-we-regulate?utm_source=substack&utm_campaign=post_embed&utm_medium=web">https://www.noahpinion.blog/p/if-ai-is-a-weapon-why-dont-we-regulate?utm_source=substack&utm_campaign=post_embed&utm_medium=web</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://arnoldkling.substack.com/p/ai-links-3142026">AI Links, 3/14/2026</a></p>]]></description><link>https://www.noahpinion.blog/p/if-ai-is-a-weapon-why-dont-we-regulate?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_campaign=post_embed&amp;u